WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.335
Here’s Sandbox Builder in Everruns.

2
00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.820
Start from an existing Sandbox Template.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.429
Choose the provider account and the base
computer.

4
00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:10.989
This first version builds Daytona
snapshots.

5
00:00:11.689 --> 00:00:14.019
The recipe is just an install script.

6
00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:17.609
Install the tools you need, without a
catalog of presets.

7
00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:20.977
Verification and software notes are
optional.

8
00:00:20.977 --> 00:00:23.349
Build access can allow package downloads

9
00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:25.602
while runtime access stays restricted.

10
00:00:26.302 --> 00:00:28.847
Everruns installs the software, creates a

11
00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:31.577
snapshot, then checks it in a fresh
sandbox.

12
00:00:32.277 --> 00:00:35.463
The result includes logs and readable
software notes.

13
00:00:35.463 --> 00:00:37.927
Temporary build computers are cleaned up.

14
00:00:38.627 --> 00:00:40.750
Save a new revision when it’s ready.

15
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.346
Existing agents and sessions keep their
pinned configuration.

16
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:46.986
Use that revision for new work.

17
00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:51.241
Your tools are baked in; workload
credentials never enter the build.
